#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
MCP Julia REPL Adapter (multiplexing router)

This adapter is the MCP server as far as the client (Claude Code, Gemini, ...) is
concerned. It is launched once per project session over stdio, with its working
directory set to the project the agent is working in.

Multiple Julia REPLs can run at once, each on its own port, each advertising
itself with a `<pid>.json` file in ~/.mcprepl/registry/. This adapter discovers
those REPLs and routes every `tools/call` to the correct one:

  * exactly one REPL, or a unique nearest-ancestor of our cwd  -> route silently
  * otherwise, or when a strictly-nearer REPL appears          -> ask the USER
    which REPL to use, via MCP elicitation (no LLM involved)
  * if the client does not support elicitation                 -> return a
    "pick a REPL, retry with repl=<word>" message to the caller instead

Julia stays a plain HTTP request/response endpoint; all routing lives here.

The Julia REPL server(s) must be running first:
    julia --project -e "using MCPRepl; MCPRepl.start!()"
"""

